  Mutation tests  (assertion-strength validation)
==============================================================================

  Strategy: replace each named fact's body with `{}` (no constraint),
  then re-run Alloy. Each listed assertion should now FAIL on the
  mutated model. If it still PASSes, the assertion is vacuous and
  must be strengthened.

  - MUTATE F_LeastPrivilegeOperations  → runs/A-L2/mutated_F_LeastPrivilegeOperations.als
    rationale: Clearing F_LeastPrivilegeOperations removes the structural constraint that every Operation's (role, kind) lies in the permission matrix. The injection forces an Operation whose (role, kind) is NOT in PermMatrix.Allowed — a direct counterexample to LeastPrivilege and every role-scope FR derived from the matrix.
    expected to FAIL: LeastPrivilege, FR_001_AuthRequired, FR_002_CustomerScope, FR_003_OfficerScope, FR_004_ComplianceReadOnly, FR_023_ComplianceNoWrite, AuthRequiredEverywhere
      - LeastPrivilege: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_001_AuthRequired: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_002_CustomerScope: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_003_OfficerScope: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_004_ComplianceReadOnly: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_023_ComplianceNoWrite: FAIL (expected)
      - AuthRequiredEverywhere: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AuditAppendOnlyNoDup  → runs/A-L2/mutated_F_AuditAppendOnlyNoDup.als
    rationale: Clearing F_AuditAppendOnlyNoDup permits duplicate audit entries for the same (application, newStatus) transition. The injection forces two distinct AuditEntries to cover the same applied transition — exactly what AppendOnly forbids.
    expected to FAIL: AppendOnly, FR_018_AppendOnly, FR_019_OnePerTransition, AuditCompleteness
      - AppendOnly: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_018_AppendOnly: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_019_OnePerTransition: PASS (vacuous?)
      - AuditCompleteness: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_AuditCompleteness  → runs/A-L2/mutated_F_AuditCompleteness.als
    rationale: Clearing F_AuditCompleteness allows applications to exist without their mandatory submission audit entry. The injection forces a LoanApplication with no Submitted-newStatus AuditEntry, breaking the 'every applied transition has exactly one audit entry' invariant.
    expected to FAIL: AuditCompleteness, FR_017_AuditMandatory, FR_019_OnePerTransition, FR_009_SubmissionAudited
      - AuditCompleteness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_017_AuditMandatory: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_019_OnePerTransition: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_009_SubmissionAudited: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_OwnershipBasedAccess  → runs/A-L2/mutated_F_OwnershipBasedAccess.als
    rationale: Clearing F_OwnershipBasedAccess removes the cross-tenant check that constrains customer-role Operations to applications they own. The injection forces a customer Operation whose target is owned by a different customer — exactly the FR-020 'no other-customer access' violation.
    expected to FAIL: OwnershipBasedAccess, FR_020_CustomerOwnOnly
      - OwnershipBasedAccess: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_020_CustomerOwnOnly: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_DecisionPostConditions  → runs/A-L2/mutated_F_DecisionPostConditions.als
    rationale: Clearing F_DecisionPostConditions removes the rule that decidedBy must equal the application's assignedOfficer. The injection forces a Decision whose decider is not the assigned officer — the canonical FR-013 violation that the conditional UPDATE in service.py is built to prevent.
    expected to FAIL: FR_013_AssignedOfficerDecides
      - FR_013_AssignedOfficerDecides: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_OneInFlightPerCustomer  → runs/A-L2/mutated_F_OneInFlightPerCustomer.als
    rationale: Clearing F_OneInFlightPerCustomer disables the partial unique index that prevents two simultaneous in-flight applications per customer. The injection constructs two distinct applications for the same customer, both in Submitted/Under Review — exactly the FR-008 violation that triggers 409 has_in_flight_application in service.py.
    expected to FAIL: FR_008_OneInFlight
      - FR_008_OneInFlight: FAIL (expected)

